    "media:imagetext": "WESTERN AIRLINES\nINTERNATIONAL\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nYou are flying aboard an aircraft with a Flight Crew which\nis thoroughly trained and experienced. It is extremely\nunlikely that certain safety facilities will be needed, but\nsimply as a precaution we would like you to be familiar with\nthese features.\nSEAT BELTS\nEven if the \"SEAT BELT\" sign is turned off in flight, it is\nrecommended that you keep your seat belt loosely fastened,\nwhenever you are in your seat.\nSEATBACKS\nFederal Aviation Regulations require your seatback to be\nupright during taxi, take off and landing.\nNO SMOKING\nWhen the \"NO SMOKING\" sign is off, you may smoke\ncigarettes while seated anywhere in the Cabin. Whenever\nthe \"NO SMOKING\" sign comes on, however, all cigarettes\nare to be extinguished.\nHAND LUGGAGE\nFederal Aviation Regulations require any article of baggage\ncarried aboard to be placed under a passenger seat.\nLIFE VESTS\nBRACE POSITIONS\nIn the event of a water\nlanding, life vests are\nFORWARD\nFACING SEAT\nAFT FACING\nSEAT\nprovided under each\nseat. Clear instructions\nfor use are contained in\nthe vest storage packet\nFEDERAL AVIATION REGULATIONS\nNo person shall drink any alcoholic beverage aboard an\nair carrier aircraft unless such beverage has been served\nto him by the air carrier operating the aircraft.\nNo air carrier shall serve any alcoholic beverage to any\nperson aboard air carrier aircaft if such person appears to\nbe intoxicated.\nNo air carrier shall permit any person to board an air\ncarrier aircraft if such person appears to be intoxicated.\nAlcoholic beverages cannot be served to minors.\nPORTABLE RADIOS\nFederal Aviation Regulation Part 91.19 permits only the\nfollowing Portable Electronic devices to be operated aboard\nAir Carrier aircraft:\n1.\nPortable voice recorders.\n2. Hearing aids.\n3. Heart pacemakers.\nElectric shavers or\nAny other portable electronic devices that Western's\nCommunications Department has determined will not\ninterfere with the aircraft Navigation or Communica-\ntions systems.\nOperation of Portable FM Radios is expressly prohibited.\nPLEASE SEE OTHER SIDE",
